<title>PORTUGAL: Portugal 7-yr floater dips to 9,946.35 esc.</title>
<headline>Portugal 7-yr floater dips to 9,946.35 esc.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is the result of today's auction of seven-year Portuguese floating rate bonds, whose average weighted price fell 6.58 escudos to 9,946.35 escudos.</p>
<p>ENTITY: Portuguese government</p>
<p>AMOUNT OFFERED: 25 bln esc</p>
<p>AMOUNT PLACED: 25 bln esc</p>
<p>INDEXED TO: six-month Lisbor minus 25 bp</p>
<p>MATURITY: 30 July 2004</p>
<p>DENOMINATION: 10</p>
<p>PAYMENT DATE: 27 May 1997</p>
<p>PAYMENT COUPON: every six months</p>
<p>AVERAGE WEIGHTED PRICE: 9,946.35 esc</p>
<p>MAXIMUM PRICE: 9,965.00 esc</p>
<p>MINIMUM PRICE: 9,940.50 esc</p>
<p>DEMAND: 47.34 bln esc</p>
<p>ISSUE FUNGIBLE WITH: OTRV/97/04</p>
<p>ESTIMATE OF TOTAL ISSUED: 93.07 bln esc</p>
<p>S &amp; P: AAA</p>
<p>-- Lisbon newsroom +351-1-3538254</p>
</text>
